===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ḱerd-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|accord}}, from {{der|en|fro|acort}}, from {{m|fro|acorder}} (see [[#Etymology 2|verb below]]).<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=accō̆rd|pos=n|id=MED289}}</ref><ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=3835341814}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# Agreement or [[concurrence]] of opinion, will, or action.
#* {{RQ:KJV|Acts|1|14|passage=These all continued with one '''accord''' in prayer and supplication, with the women, and Mary the mother of Iesus, and with his brethen.}}
#* {{RQ:Bacon Henry 7|passage=a mediator of an '''accord''' and peace between them}}
# A [[harmony]] in sound, [[pitch]] and [[tone]]; [[concord]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=17th century|title=The Self-Subsistence of the Soul|author=[[w:John Davies (poet)|Sir John Davies]]|passage=Those sweet '''accords''' are even the angels' lays.}}
# Agreement or harmony of things in general.
#: {{ux|en|the '''accord''' of light and shade in painting}}
# {{lb|en|countable|perfumery}} A distinctive mixture of [[fragrance]]s or the [[odor]] thereof.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Daphna Havkin-Frenkel; Faith C. Belanger|title=Handbook of Vanilla Science and Technology|publisher=John Wiley & Sons|isbn=9781444329377
|text=Oriental fragrances often incorporate an '''accord''' referred to as amber. It is a perfumery '''accord''' using vanilla, olibanum, balsamic resins, and citrus to varying degrees.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Luca Turin; Tania Sanchez|title=Perfumes: The A–Z Guide|publisher=Profile Books|isbn=9781847651525|page=22|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=8a-Q0uZU9o8C&lpg=PA233&dq=%22oud%22%20perfume&hl=fr&pg=PA22#v=onepage&q=accord&f=false|text=Fougères are built on an '''accord''' between lavender and coumarin, with every conceivable variation and elaboration.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Valerie Ann Worwood|title=The Complete Book of Essential Oils and Aromatherapy, Revised and Expanded: Over 800 Natural, Nontoxic, and Fragrant Recipes to Create Health, Beauty, and Safe Home and Work Environments|publisher=New World Library|isbn=9781608684267|page=450
|text='''Accord''' is the perfumer's word for a perfume formulation that can be incorporated into any perfume calling for a particular note.}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} An agreement between parties in [[controversy]], by which satisfaction for an injury is [[stipulated]], and which, when [[executed]], prevents a lawsuit.
#* {{RQ:Blackstone Commentaries|passage='''Accord''' is a satisfaction agreed upon between the party injuring and the party injured ; which , when performed , is a bar of all actions upon this account}}
# {{lb|en|international law}} An international agreement.
#: {{ux|en|The Geneva '''Accord''' of 1954 ended the French-Indochinese War.}}
# Voluntary or spontaneous impulse to act.
#: {{ux|en|Nobody told me to do it. I did it of my own '''accord'''.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Leviticus|25|5|passage=That which groweth of its own '''accord''' of thy harvest thou shalt not reap.}}

